<p>In Arab, people talk. If we do a good job, you'll tell your friends. If we do a bad job, you'll tell everyone. That accountability keeps us honest — and it means you can ask around about our work before calling. Check our <a href="/recent-projects/">recent projects</a> to see work we've done in the area.</p>

<h4>When Things Need Attention in Arab</h4>
<p><strong>Spring:</strong> After winter's freeze-thaw cycles, check for any damage. Mountain areas experience more ice events than the valley, and ice can lift gutters and stress seams. Press on fascia boards — don't just look at them.</p>

<p><strong>After storms:</strong> Arab gets the same severe weather as Huntsville, but tree damage can be worse in the heavily wooded mountain areas. Walk your property after significant storms.</p>

<p><strong>Fall:</strong> Leaf drop often starts earlier at higher elevations. Don't wait until November to think about gutter cleaning — Arab's trees may finish dropping by late October.</p>

<h4>What's Different About Mountain Homes</h4>
<ul>
<li>Gutters work harder on sloped roofs — water hits at higher velocity</li>
<li>Underground drainage may require working around rock (adds 20-30% to cost)</li>
<li>Higher morning fog and moisture affects fascia wear</li>
<li>Ice events are more common than in the valley — proper hanger spacing (24 inches) matters</li>
